## Better — Your Stack Approach

```python
class Solution:
    def compress(self, s):
        n = len(s)
        stack = []

        i = n - 1

        while i > 0:
            length = i + 1

            if length % 2 == 1:
                stack.append(s[i])
                i -= 1
                continue

            half = length // 2
            same = True

            for j in range(half):
                if s[j] != s[j + half]:
                    same = False
                    break

            if same:
                stack.append('*')
                i = half - 1
            else:
                stack.append(s[i])
                i -= 1

        ans = [s[0]]

        while stack:
            ans.append(stack.pop())

        return "".join(ans)
```

**TC:** O(n²)
**SC:** O(n)

> Your logic is correct for the intended transformation. The main problem is the repeated character comparison, which can make it **O(n²)** for `n = 10⁵`.

